<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nobel Prize</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Nobel Prizes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nobel Prizes are international awards founded under the will of the Swedish chemist and industrialist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-nobel">Alfred Nobel</a> and first awarded in 1901. They are given each year for physics, chemistry, physiology or medicine, literature and peace, and since 1969 also for economic sciences, a prize established by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s central bank. The prizes are presented in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a>, except for the peace prize, which is awarded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nobel-prize.jpg" alt="Nobel Prize" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nobel Foundation, diploma by Sofia Gisberg[1] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marie_Sk%C5%82odowska-Curie%27s_Nobel_Prize_in_Chemistry_1911.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
